stimulus.description:
A teacher is writing a class PasswordCheck with two static methods. The class is shown with the method headers. (The threshold for a long password is 6 characters.)
```java
public class PasswordCheck {
    /** Returns the number of uppercase letters (A through Z) in s. */
    public static int countUpper(String s) { /* to be implemented in part (a) */ }

    /** Rates the strength of the password s; see part (b). */
    public static String rate(String s) { /* to be implemented in part (b) */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static int countUpper(String s) {
        int count = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < s.length(); i++) {
            char ch = s.charAt(i);
            if (ch >= 'A' && ch <= 'Z') {
                count++;
            }
        }
        return count;
    }
```

One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static String rate(String s) {
        int upper = countUpper(s);
        if (s.length() >= 6 && upper >= 2) {
            return "strong";
        }
        if (s.length() >= 6 || upper >= 1) {
            return "medium";
        }
        return "weak";
    }
```

