stimulus.description:
A data-analysis class uses an ArrayList<Integer> of measurements. The class is shown with the header of the method you will write.
```java
import java.util.ArrayList;

public class DataTools {
    /** Returns a new ArrayList containing the values of data that are strictly greater than the average
     *  of all values in data, in their original order. The list data is not modified.
     *  Returns an empty list if data is empty. */
    public static ArrayList<Integer> aboveAverage(ArrayList<Integer> data) { /* to be written */ }
}
```

parts.model_answer:
One correct implementation (ALTON reference answer):
```java
    public static ArrayList<Integer> aboveAverage(ArrayList<Integer> data) {
        ArrayList<Integer> result = new ArrayList<Integer>();
        if (data.size() == 0) {
            return result;
        }
        int sum = 0;
        for (int i = 0; i < data.size(); i++) {
            sum += data.get(i);
        }
        double avg = (double) sum / data.size();
        for (int i = 0; i < data.size(); i++) {
            if (data.get(i) > avg) {
                result.add(data.get(i));
            }
        }
        return result;
    }
```

